1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,434
Small law firms lose clients in the intake form.

2
00:00:03,484 --> 00:00:07,545
Older clients, people at work, anyone reading a second language.

3
00:00:07,595 --> 00:00:08,894
They don't finish it.

4
00:00:08,944 --> 00:00:13,070
So we made the form three steps, and let the phone do the intake.

5
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,546
This is Not-a-Lawyer Intake.

6
00:00:15,596 --> 00:00:16,923
Step one: pick a topic.

7
00:00:16,973 --> 00:00:19,317
Real estate, a will, a trust, a lawsuit.

8
00:00:19,367 --> 00:00:26,081
That choice plans the call: a lawsuit intake asks who the other side is and what deadline is on the court papers;

9
00:00:26,131 --> 00:00:28,954
a will intake asks about family and an executor.

10
00:00:29,004 --> 00:00:30,630
Step two: leave your number.

11
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:39,070
The interview language follows the phone's country, straight from CALL-E's region table, and the page says plainly what your number supports.

12
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:49,670
Submit, and the page tells you exactly what happens next: your phone rings in about a minute, what the assistant will ask, and what the firm does afterward.

13
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:57,442
This is the real lawsuit call, recorded on the client's phone, abridged.

14
00:00:57,492 --> 00:00:59,364
Not legal advice comes first.

15
00:00:59,414 --> 00:01:03,076
Then the matter: the form said court papers had arrived;

16
00:01:03,126 --> 00:01:08,643
the client says no lawsuit yet, so the assistant records him as the one bringing it.

17
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:10,830
Then the email, letter by letter.

18
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:50,013
Thirty seconds after the call, the staff console has this.

19
00:01:50,063 --> 00:01:57,405
Summary, the other parties for the conflict check, urgency, consent, transcript, and CALL-E's confidence score.

20
00:01:57,455 --> 00:02:04,597
Each topic gets its own column of fields, and a date picker places a reminder call in the client's language.

21
00:02:04,647 --> 00:02:11,190
Staff can also start an intake call from the desk, for a walk-in or a voicemail, and watch it land.

22
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,296
Same number, different language.

23
00:02:14,346 --> 00:02:18,907
This is the Bahasa Indonesia call, also real, also on a US line.

24
00:02:18,957 --> 00:02:23,590
Adding a language is one row in a JSON file and one script block.

25
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,065
One limit, stated plainly.

26
00:02:26,115 --> 00:02:29,028
CALL-E does not carry Spanish on US lines yet.

27
00:02:29,078 --> 00:02:32,635
We tried the locale, the task text, and the MCP planner;

28
00:02:32,685 --> 00:02:34,825
all three declined before dialing.

29
00:02:34,875 --> 00:02:37,401
The Spanish script is written and wired.

30
00:02:37,451 --> 00:02:41,910
Until it's enabled, those callers go to a human, and the form says so.

31
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,369
No servers.

32
00:02:43,419 --> 00:02:51,876
Cloudflare Pages, a few Functions, KV, and the CALL-E API: a task and a result schema planned per matter type, webhooks, and idempotency keys.

33
00:02:51,926 --> 00:02:54,393
Repo and live link are in the description.

34
00:02:54,443 --> 00:02:56,070
This is Not-a-Lawyer Intake.
